project/browser-witness-cdp-fallback: when the gm browser verb extension bridge is not connected, witness via external CDP: launch headless chrome ("/c/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe" --headless=new --remote-debugging-port=9223 --user-data-dir=/tmp/x about:blank &), then dispatch browser body line `session new --direct localhost:9223` to mint a session, then header-less JS bodies (page global) run against it. Pitfalls: 14s execution cap (split nav and probe into separate dispatches); the watcher pins .gm/exec-spool/browser-sessions.json default:[ID] and stale pins route header-less bodies to a dead session (clear browser-sessions.json to {default:[]} + browser-ports.json to {} to reset); chrome can hit ERR_NETWORK_IO_SUSPENDED when idle or a libuv UV_HANDLE_CLOSING assertion under the relay — relaunch on a fresh port.